# Relune — Environment template

Copy to `.env` for local development.

## Core
```bash
# Postgres (recommended — start with: docker compose up postgres redis -d)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://relune:relune@localhost:5432/relune?schema=public"

AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string-min-32-chars"
AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
# MAINTENANCE_MODE=false
```

## OAuth (optional — leave blank to disable that button until configured)
## Supported: Google, Apple, Facebook, X (Twitter). No other providers.
```bash
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
AUTH_APPLE_ID=
AUTH_APPLE_SECRET=
AUTH_FACEBOOK_ID=
AUTH_FACEBOOK_SECRET=
AUTH_TWITTER_ID=
AUTH_TWITTER_SECRET=
# AUTH_X_ID=        # alias for Twitter/X
# AUTH_X_SECRET=
```

## Cache / realtime (recommended for production)
```bash
REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
```

## Email
```bash
# Development: log previews to console
MAIL_PROVIDER=log

# Production (required):
# MAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM="Relune <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
```

## SMS (phone login / verification)
```bash
SMS_PROVIDER=log
# SMS_PROVIDER=twilio
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=+15551234567
```

## Analytics (client)
```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=none
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=plausible
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=yourdomain.com
```

## Demo seeds (never enable in production)
```bash
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEEDS=false
```

## Media uploads
Local uploads are stored under `public/uploads/` (gitignored). Optional CDN keys for future workers:
```bash
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
```

## WebRTC / calls (optional TURN for restrictive NATs)
```bash
# Comma-separated TURN URLs, e.g. turn:turn.example.com:3478?transport=udp
# TURN_URLS=turn:turn.example.com:3478
# Shared secret for time-limited REST credentials (coturn static-auth-secret)
# TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-turn-shared-secret
```

## Web Push (optional — generate with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys)
```bash
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:noreply@yourdomain.com
```

## Session lifetime (days)
```bash
# SESSION_DAYS=30
```

## Production block (copy into host secrets / Compose / Fly / Render)
```bash
NODE_ENV=production
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://relune:STRONG_PASSWORD@db-host:5432/relune?schema=public"
REDIS_URL="redis://:STRONG_PASSWORD@redis-host:6379"
AUTH_SECRET="generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-48"
AUTH_URL="https://app.yourdomain.com"
NEXTAUTH_URL="https://app.yourdomain.com"
MAIL_PROVIDER=resend
RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
MAIL_FROM="Relune <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# MAINTENANCE_MODE=false
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEEDS=false
```

## Capacitor (native shells — not required by the Node server)
```bash
# Used only when syncing iOS/Android projects:
# CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL="https://app.yourdomain.com"
```
